course: dictionary
lesson: 11220
title: Woodland
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Woodland is land covered with trees, an area of woods. The clues come from the sentence «Lions live on savanna, grassland and open woodland in Africa.» Lions live on grassy land, so woodland must be another kind of place where animals can live.
explain: Woodland is usually smaller and more open than a forest. If you read about a forest, picture a bigger, thicker place full of trees.
explain: The sentence «Lions do not live in jungles» also helps. Woodland is not the same as a jungle. It is a place with trees, but it can be more open, with more space between the trees.
fact: Woodland means land covered with trees, an area of woods.
fact: Woodland is usually smaller and more open than a forest.
fact: Woodland is a habitat, a home, for animals like deer, badgers, foxes, owls and squirrels.
fact: Woodland plants often grow in the shade under the trees.
fact: Phrases to know: woodland walk, woodland animals, ancient woodland, woodland floor.
exercise: «Lions live on savanna, grassland and open woodland in Africa.» What is woodland? | A hot desert with no plants | A huge sea of water | A stone wall built around a town | *Land covered with trees
exercise: Woodland is usually smaller and more open than what? | A garden shed | A pond | A river | *A forest
exercise: Which animal might you find living in woodland? | A penguin on the ice | A whale in the sea | *A badger | A camel in the desert
test: Why should you stay on paths and with an adult on a woodland walk? | To find the biggest tree | To make the most noise you can | *To keep safe and not get lost | To pick every flower you see
test: Woodland plants often grow in which place? | *In the shade | Under the ice | In deep water | In bright sun on open sea
exam: Which phrase names the ground under the trees in a wood? | ancient woodland | *woodland floor | woodland walk | woodland animals
